<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Serbia farmers can pay taxes with 1997 wheat-paper.</title>
<headline>Serbia farmers can pay taxes with 1997 wheat-paper.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Serbian farmers will be able to pay their taxes with wheat from this year's crop, the Belgrade daily Politika reported on Friday.</p>
<p>According to a decision taken by the Serbian government at its last session, the wheat will be handed to the Serbian Commodity Reserve Agency through authorised warehouses.</p>
<p>The Agency then takes over the tax debt and must pay to Serbia's public revenues office 35 percent of the value of the wheat within eight days, 25 percent in 45 days and 20 percent each in 60 and 90 days respectively. -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom + 381 11 311 4305</p>
</text>
